              (set! (.-abs (.-b z)) (.lsh (.-abs (.-b z)) (.-abs (.-b z)) (conv uint (- exp2)))))


            (set! (.-neg (.-a z)) (and neg (> (len (.-abs (.-a z))) 0))) ; 0 has no sign

            (return (.norm z) true)))))))


















^{:go/end 301} (go/func scanExponent "scanExponent scans the longest possible prefix of r representing a base 10\n(“e”, “E”) or a base 2 (“p”, “P”) exponent, if any. It returns the\nexponent, the exponent base (10 or 2), or a read or syntax error, if any.\n\nIf sepOk is set, an underscore character “_” may appear between successive\nexponent digits; such underscores do not change the value of the exponent.\nIncorrect placement of underscores is reported as an error if there are no\nother errors. If sepOk is not set, underscores are not recognized and thus\nterminate scanning like any other character that is not a valid digit.\n\n\texponent = ( \"e\" | \"E\" | \"p\" | \"P\" ) [ sign ] digits .\n\tsign     = \"+\" | \"-\" .\n\tdigits   = digit { [ '_' ] digit } .\n\tdigit    = \"0\" ... \"9\" .\n\nA base 2 exponent is only permitted if base2ok is set.\n" [^io/ByteScanner r ^bool base2ok ^bool sepOk] :results [^int64 exp ^int base ^error err]
  ;; one char look-ahead
  (let [(values ch ^:assign err) (.ReadByte r)]
    (when (!= err nil)
      (when (== err io/EOF)
        (set! err nil))

      (return 0 10 err))


    ;; exponent char
    (switch ch
      (case [\e \E]
        (set! base 10))
      (case [\p \P]
        (when base2ok
          (set! base 2)
          (break)) ; ok

        (fallthrough)) ; binary exponent not permitted
      (default
        (.UnreadByte r) ; ch does not belong to exponent anymore
        (return 0 10 nil)))


    ;; sign
    (let [^{:tag (slice byte)} digits (zero (slice byte))]
      (set! (values ch err) (.ReadByte r))
      (when (and (== err nil) ^:go/paren (or (== ch \+) (== ch \-)))
        (when (== ch \-)
          (set! digits (append digits \-)))

        (set! (values ch err) (.ReadByte r)))


      ;; prev encodes the previously seen char: it is one
      ;; of '_', '0' (a digit), or '.' (anything else). A
      ;; valid separator '_' may only occur after a digit.
      (let [prev \.
          ^{:line 265} invalSep false

          ;; exponent value
          ^{:line 268} hasDigits false]
        (while (== err nil)
          (cond (and (<= \0 ch) (<= ch \9)) (do
              (set! digits (append digits ch))
              (set! prev \0)
              (set! hasDigits true))
            (and (== ch \_) sepOk) (do
              (when (!= prev \0)
                (set! invalSep true))

              (set! prev \_)) :else
            (do
              (.UnreadByte r) ; ch does not belong to number anymore
              (break)))

          (set! (values ch err) (.ReadByte r)))


        (when (== err io/EOF)
          (set! err nil))

        (when (and (== err nil) (not hasDigits))
          (set! err errNoDigits))

        (when (== err nil)
          (set! (values exp err) (strconv/ParseInt (conv string digits) 10 64)))

        ;; other errors take precedence over invalid separators
        (when (and (== err nil) ^:go/paren (or invalSep (== prev \_)))
          (set! err errInvalSep))


        (return)))))



^{:go/end 306} (go/method String "String returns a string representation of x in the form \"a/b\" (even if b == 1).\n" ^string [^{:tag (* Rat)} x]
  (conv string (.marshal x nil)))





^{:go/end 320} (go/method marshal "marshal implements [Rat.String] returning a slice of bytes.\nIt appends the string representation of x in the form \"a/b\" (even if b == 1) to buf,\nand returns the extended buffer.\n" ^{:tag (slice byte)} [^{:tag (* Rat)} x ^{:tag (slice byte)} buf]
  (set! buf (.Append (.-a x) buf 10))
  (set! buf (append buf \/))
  (if (!= (len (.-abs (.-b x))) 0)
    (set! buf (.Append (.-b x) buf 10))

    (set! buf (append buf \1)))

  ^{:line 319} buf)




^{:go/end 329} (go/method RatString "RatString returns a string representation of x in the form \"a/b\" if b != 1,\nand in the form \"a\" if b == 1.\n" ^string [^{:tag (* Rat)} x]
  (when (.IsInt x)
    (return (.String (.-a x))))

  (.String x))





^{:go/end 386} (go/method FloatString "FloatString returns a string representation of x in decimal form with prec\ndigits of precision after the radix point. The last digit is rounded to\nnearest, with halves rounded away from zero.\n" ^string [^{:tag (* Rat)} x ^int prec]
  (let [^{:tag (slice byte)} buf (zero (slice byte))]

    (when (.IsInt x)
      (set! buf (.Append (.-a x) buf 10))
      (when (> prec 0)
        (set! buf (append buf \.))
        (for [i prec] (> i 0) (dec! i)
          (set! buf (append buf \0))))


      (return (conv string buf)))

    ;; x.b.abs != 0

    (let [stk (getStack)]
      (defer (.free stk))
      (let [(values q r) (.div (conv nat nil) stk (conv nat nil) (.-abs (.-a x)) (.-abs (.-b x)))

          ^{:line 353} p natOne]
